================================================================================
5. PROPOSED BREAKDOWN
================================================================================

Ordered cheapest-first. Each layer is independently useful.

A. ASSET TYPE REGISTRY                                          BUILT, DIFFERENTLY
   THIS ASKED TO "replace free-text asset_type with a controlled vocabulary".
   THE VOCABULARY EXISTS AND IS DERIVED RATHER THAN TYPED, which is better
   than what was asked for:

     * assetTypeOf(filename) in shared/assetRules.mjs classifies every file
       against TYPE_BY_EXTENSION — the controlled vocabulary.
     * The client does NOT send asset_type at all, deliberately: the field
       asked a human to choose between content types and TOOLS, and the tool
       is a property of the file a verifier can read.
     * The technical check RECORDS the type when every file in the version
       agrees, with COALESCE so an ambiguous version cannot wipe a type an
       earlier version established.
     * The server stopped accepting asset_type from the request entirely
       (2026-10-23), so there is one way to set it and no dead second one.

   WHAT IS STILL MISSING FROM THIS PARAGRAPH: "required companions" per type,
   and the vetting-gate rules below (polygon limits, texture dimensions,
   naming conventions, format compliance). Only the format-compliance gate is
   genuinely absent — the content checks exist.

B. DOWNLOAD TO LOCAL WORKING COPY                               SMALL
   ZIP preserving relative_path (which exists in the schema for exactly this)
   plus a JSON manifest: per-file SHA-256, size, and target path. The approver
   has a working copy of the game, so files must land in the right places.
   A small CLI later lets an artist sync by hash instead of re-downloading.
   HIGHEST VALUE, LOWEST RISK. Unblocks approval review immediately.
   SECURITY: this is the first code that serves user-uploaded bytes.
     - Use application/octet-stream + Content-Disposition: attachment.
       NEVER the stored mime_type, or an uploaded .svg/.html becomes stored
       XSS on this origin.
     - Resolve bytes only from stored_files.storage_key; validate it is exactly
       64 hex chars before touching the filesystem. Never build a path from
       client input.
     - Re-validate relative_path at zip time. It was normalised on upload, but
       it originated client-side and is now being used to build entry names.

C. PREVIEW, TIERED BY WHAT IS ACTUALLY RENDERABLE                MEDIUM
   BUILT 2026-10-29 for the first two rows, except glTF; TODO 89.

     images (.png/.jpg/.exr/.tga)  DONE — a 320px WebP. sharp reads the common
                                   formats; TGA and EXR go through ffmpeg.
                                   The browser is sent OUR WebP with an
                                   image/webp type and nosniff, never the
                                   developer's bytes or their mime.
     video                         DONE — a frame at 1s, or 0s if the clip is
                                   shorter, through the same encoder.
     .glb/.gltf                    three.js viewer. Real 3D, cheap. NOT BUILT.
     .blend/.nk/.ma/.uasset        none render in a browser. Options:
                                   artist-uploaded renders, offline conversion
                                   to GLB (Blender does this headlessly), or
                                   download-only for now — which is where it
                                   stands.

D. THE "SEE IT IN THE GAME" LAYER                               LARGE
   Pick one of the three options in 3.2. If turntables: an OFFLINE render
   pipeline, not a web feature.

E. DISTRIBUTION VIA GIT                                         LARGE
   The spec's actual answer for 02.6. Partial plumbing exists in
   routes/superuser.js.

